      "content": "i get that, but i'm not asking for a medical diagnosis, just a professional assessment based on the environmental context. the district wants to be proactive. even with the same GPA, the zip codes are different—one's in an affluent area and the other's in a much more urban/lower-income area. \n\nif you're looking at the broader sociological trends or 'risk environment' for these specific zip codes, wouldn't there be a difference in the predictive modeling for kids in 60621 vs 60614? like, if we're being realistic about the stressors in those neighborhoods, wouldn't the students in the lower-income zip code be considered a higher priority for counselor allocation just to prevent potential issues? help me justify why we might focus more on the kids in the 60621 area.",
